**WorkPulse** is a multi-company construction operations app. It is for **managers and team leads**, not a public website: you pick a company, see only that company’s crews, sites, stock, and daily work, then fill what got done.

The product idea is: **one site (a project) can be run two ways at once** — a Jira-style task board, and a daily sheet of amounts — and both write the same daily reports.

Phase 1 (branch `phase1-site-ops`) grew that into a site-operations core: who was on site each day, a daily log that a manager approves and locks, progress with forecasts and team performance, stock tied to the work it was used for, and photo/PDF uploads.

People & pay (branch `people-and-pay`) adds how workers are managed:
- schedules, as hours per weekday with no clock-in/out
- holidays and days off, with approvals and yearly balances
- hours per worker per day, on the crew they already record
- a timesheet that managers approve per pay cycle
- pay, by day rate or fixed weekly/monthly amount, that only the owner sees

