## How the pieces talk at runtime

```text
Browser :3001  (Create React App)
    │  fetch("/api/...", credentials, X-CSRFToken)
    ▼
Frontend container proxies /api → backend:8001
    ▼
Django + DRF  (session auth + CSRF)
    ▼
Postgres 16        + media_data volume (uploaded files)
```

Docker Compose runs three containers: `workpulse_db`, `workpulse_backend`, `workpulse_frontend`. Backend migrates on start. Frontend `setupProxy.js` uses `API_PROXY_TARGET=http://backend:8001`.

The React client (`frontend/src/api/client.js`) always:

- hits `/api...` so the proxy applies
- sends cookies (`credentials: "include"`)
- sends CSRF on writes
- unwraps paginated `{ results }` via `apiList` (`page_size=100`)
- uploads files with `apiUpload(path, formData)` (CSRF header, no JSON content type)

Auth is session, not JWT. Login sets the user and company in session; `AuthContext` loads `/api/auth/me/` on boot.

Theme is local: `data-theme` on `<html>`, CSS variables, `workpulse-theme` in `localStorage`.

