## How progress and material numbers are computed

All of this is plain functions over the fact rows. Nothing is stored.

**Pace and forecast** (`operations/progress.py`)

- daily rate = quantity in the last 10 working days (Mon–Fri) ÷ 10
- forecast finish = today + remaining ÷ daily rate, counted in working days
- planned finish = project start (or first report) + the scope's length
- worker-days come from `CrewAttendance`. If a team reported two work types on one day, its worker-days are split by each report's share of the day.
- output per worker-day = quantity ÷ worker-days (only for reports where crew was recorded); per team-day is always available
- status, worst first: `behind` (forecast after planned finish), `stalled` (started, nothing in 10 working days), `no_plan`, `on_track`, `not_started`, `done`

Endpoints: `GET /api/projects/{id}/progress/`, `GET /api/teams/{id}/performance/?from&to`, `GET /api/progress/` (company overview; leads see only their projects).

**Material use** (`inventory/usage.py`)

- expected = done × norm
- actual = consume movements tagged with that scope
- variance = actual − expected (a gap points to waste or missing records)
- still needed = remaining × norm
- shortage = still needed − stock at the site location
- consumes with no work type show separately as "unassigned use"

Endpoint: `GET /api/projects/{id}/materials/`. Shown on the project Stock tab.

**Missing reports** (`sitelog/services.py`)
`GET /api/daily-logs/missing/?date=` lists teams placed on an active project that day with no report from that team. Shown on the Home page.

**Timesheet** (`timesheets/sheet.py`)

- expected hours = the schedule's hours that weekday, 0 on holidays and outside employment
- work value of a day = 0 with no hours, ½ up to half a full day, 1 above that. It uses the day's total across projects and other work, so two projects in one day count once.
- day off used = min(day-off value, 1 − work value), so working on a day off is never counted twice; the day is flagged instead
- extra hours = hours above expected (after a half day off, above half), day by day
- missing = a past scheduled day with no hours and no day off
- vacation balance = allowance − approved vacation days (days split at New Year)

**Pay** (`payroll/calc.py`, pure functions over the timesheet rows)

- **Day rate:**
  - each worked day × rate (a half day earns half)
  - paid days off × rate
  - holidays on scheduled weekdays × rate, if the company pays them and the day isn't inside an unpaid day off
  - extra hours = hours above a full day × rate ÷ full day × multiplier
- **Fixed weekly / monthly:** for each week or month, amount × scheduled days earned ÷ all scheduled days in that whole week or month (holidays included).
  - Unpaid days off, and holidays inside them, come off.
  - Scheduled days with nothing recorded are still paid, and shown.
  - Extra hours = hours above the schedule (every hour on an unscheduled day) × amount ÷ scheduled hours that week or month × multiplier.
  - A hire on the 15th earns about half a month.
- Amounts keep full precision and are rounded to cents once per component. Gross = base + extra + days off + holidays + bonuses; net = gross − deductions; to pay = owed before + net.

